  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for Management (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 15+15+15+15+16+14+15+15 = 120 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 120). The program is a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA; the plan lists the Common Professional Component requirements). Sophomore year has flexible 'or Elective' options: ECO1401/MGT2400/MIS1300 can be taken in Fall with electives in Spring, or vice versa — transcribed as printed. Junior Fall and Senior Spring each include 'MGT3XXX, any 3000 level business course' (6 credits total of 3000-level or higher business electives). Management major requirements: ECO2210 Labor Economics, ECO4200 Economics of Managerial Decisions, IBS3820 Global Supply Chain and International Negotiations, MGT2400 Organizational Behavior, MGT3201 Business and Society, MGT3202 Leadership, MGT3213 Human Resource Management, MGT3661 Project Management, plus 6 credits of 3000-level business electives. The capstone is BUS4899 Business Internship OR MGT4800 Senior Policy Seminar (one in Senior Fall, the other in Senior Spring — both are Common Professional Component requirements, transcribed as printed). General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202/ENG1602 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
